---
import SiteFooter from '../components/navigation/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/navigation/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactLine from '../components/ui/ContactLine.astro';
import { legalLastUpdated, siteCreator } from '../content/site';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/navigation/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { pageBreadcrumbs } from '../content/seo';
const breadcrumbs = pageBreadcrumbs('Privacy', '/privacy/');
---

<BaseLayout canonical="/privacy/" title="Privacy | GraphMaker" description="How GraphMaker handles graph data in the browser." robots="noindex,follow" breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <SiteHeader hasEditor={false} hasFaq={false} />
  <main class="page-shell max-w-4xl py-10 sm:py-14" id="main-content">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
    {legalLastUpdated && <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 text-sm">Last updated: {legalLastUpdated}</p>}
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-4 leading-7">GraphMaker’s editor processes pasted and uploaded graph data in your browser. The application does not require an account or cloud database.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mt-9">Local projects</h2><p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">When you choose Save locally, the project is stored in IndexedDB on that device. Clearing browser storage can remove locally saved projects.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mt-9">Project files and exports</h2><p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">Files you import are read by the browser. Graph images, data exports, and project files are downloaded directly to your device.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mt-9">Usage analytics</h2><p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">Google Analytics records page visits and general browser, device, and referral information. GraphMaker does not send spreadsheet cells, graph values, uploaded-file contents, project names, or exported data to Google Analytics. For Google Analytics, advertising personalization and Google signals are disabled.</p>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">Google Analytics may set cookies or similar identifiers to measure visits and distinguish browsers. These page-visit measurements are separate from your graph data, which is never sent to a GraphMaker server. The analytics script loads when a page opens.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mt-9">Google advertising services</h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">GraphMaker loads the Google AdSense script. When ads are served, third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies to serve ads based on your previous visits to this website or other websites. Google's advertising cookies allow Google and its partners to serve ads based on visits to this site and other sites on the Internet.</p>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">Advertising providers may place or read cookies and use web beacons, IP addresses, browser information, and similar identifiers to deliver and measure ads. Other third-party advertising vendors or networks may also use cookies when their ads are served. These advertising services are separate from the Google Analytics settings described above.</p>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">Learn how Google uses information from partner sites in <a class="text-brand underline" href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">Google's partner-site privacy information</a> and read <a class="text-brand underline" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mt-9">Advertising choices</h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">You can manage or opt out of Google's personalized advertising through <a class="text-brand underline" href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a>. You can also opt out of personalized advertising from participating third-party providers through <a class="text-brand underline" href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">YourAdChoices</a>. These choices do not necessarily stop all ads or the use of identifiers for purposes such as fraud prevention and measurement.</p>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">Your browser settings can block or delete cookies and other site storage. Clearing site storage can also delete GraphMaker projects saved locally; export a project file first if you need a backup.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mt-9">Site owner and contact</h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 leading-7">GraphMaker is operated by {siteCreator.name}. Learn about the creator and product on the <a class="text-brand underline" href="/about/#creator">About page</a>.</p>
    <ContactLine />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
